<BaseLayout title="About ColorCode Identifier" description="Learn about ColorCode Identifier, a free browser-based color identification and reference toolkit."><div class="container"><div class="page-hero"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / About</div><span class="eyebrow">About the project</span><h1>About ColorCode Identifier</h1><p>We make it easier to explore visible colors and understand the digital values behind them.</p></div><article class="prose"><h2>What we do</h2><p>ColorCode Identifier is a browser-based toolkit for sampling colors from photos, exploring HEX, RGB and HSL values, and learning about color references. Our initial focus includes car and motorcycle color discovery.</p><h2>Accuracy and limitations</h2><p>Our photo tools report the color values represented by image pixels. They do not identify original automotive paint formulas or guarantee a physical paint match. Lighting, camera processing, display calibration and surface finish can change perceived color.</p><h2>Our approach</h2><p>We aim to provide clear instructions, transparent limitations and practical tools that work without requiring an account.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>For questions or corrections, use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p></article></div></BaseLayout>
